@* A Modal declared inside the content of another one, which is the shape a confirmation asked for from
   inside a form takes. Each of the two keeps its own half of the dialog contract: the Escape that dismisses
   the inner one stops there, and both of them hold the page behind them until the last one closes. *@
<BitModal @bind-IsOpen="IsOuterOpen" Class="outer-modal">
    <div>
        <button class="outer-button">Outer</button>

        <BitModal @bind-IsOpen="IsInnerOpen" Class="inner-modal">
            <div>
                <button class="inner-button">Inner</button>
            </div>
        </BitModal>
    </div>
</BitModal>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool IsOuterOpen { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool IsInnerOpen { get; set; }
}
